p We are a results and data-driven organization. This allows us to avoid the bureaucracy of typical large companies. We value people who are doers instead of talkers, who obsess over the details, who listen to data yet know when to trust their gut, and who empathize with our users.

p At Nitrous, we're making programming more enjoyable and programmers and teams more productive. As a developer evangelist at Nitrous, you will interact with beginner, amateur and professional programmers to educate them on Nitrous's most powerful features, and listen to them to help us continually improve the platform.

p We are looking for developer evangelists with boundless energy who love traveling, meeting new people, and are obsessed with new technology and changing the way programmers work.

h3 Responsibilities

ul
  li Giving talks and demos of new Nitrous features at conferences
  li Writing Call for Papers and Abstracts to submit to developer conferences
  li Traveling to conferences and representing the company
  li Writing tutorials about how to use Nitrous with different technologies
  li Creating "how-to" videos and other introduction videos

h3 Requirements

ul
  li Excellent written and verbal communication skills
  li Experience with public speaking, specifically on technical topics
  li Experience demoing technical products in front of large audiences

p To apply, please provide the following:

ul
  li Github Profile with code you've written
  li Links to blog and/or videos of talks
  li Links to community profiles like Twitter, Hacker News, Stack Overflow, Reddit, etc...
  li Why you want to change development

